Description: The DJ's library data on the USB drive (DECKSMITHOS/)
 Part of the USB import (DECKSMITHOS_USB_IMPORT, patch 0016). A drive with a
 folder DECKSMITHOS/ at its root (created from the DecksmithOS system menu
 or by hand; the system mounts such a drive read-write) keeps:
 - Analysis/<sha1 of the path on the drive>.json per track of the drive:
   beat grid, keys, cues and hot cues, intro/outro, track structure, replay
   gain, color, rating and the waveforms. Written (in a low priority thread,
   temporary file, sync, rename; unchanged files are not rewritten) whenever
   the library saves such a track, so analysis done and edits made on any
   console travel with the drive. Applied when the drive appears (worker
   thread reads, GUI thread applies in small batches; a track loaded first
   gets it right before loading); it wins over the rekordbox export.
 - Playlists/*.m3u8, Crates/*.m3u8 and index.json: the playlists and crates
   created while the drive is connected (the drive that appeared last), as
   M3U8 with paths relative to the file for the tracks of the drive (any
   mount point, other players) and absolute paths for the others, kept up
   to date with their tracks, order and name. They are created in the
   library when the drive appears (after its rekordbox and Serato lists,
   editable) and deleted when it is removed; list files put there by hand
   are imported too. Crates of drives left over from a crash are deleted at
   startup (table decksmithos_drive_crates).
 EJECT (patch 0017) writes everything pending first. Audio files are never
 changed.
